# Kairo Markets: example settings file.
#
# HOW TO USE (on your own PC, never in chat):
#   1. Copy this file to a new file called .env      (copy .env.example .env)
#   2. Open .env in Notepad and fill in the values below.
#   3. Never share .env, never paste its contents anywhere, never commit it.
#      (.gitignore already blocks it, and a check before every push confirms that.)
#
# Use a brand-new wallet that holds ONLY Arc TESTNET USDC. Never use a wallet that
# has ever held real money.

# --- Arc testnet network (public, not secret) ---
ARC_TESTNET_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
ARC_TESTNET_CHAIN_ID=5042002

# --- Arc testnet USDC (public). Same address as the 6-decimal USDC token on Arc. ---
USDC_ADDRESS=0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000

# --- Deployer wallet (SECRET) ---
# The private key of the testnet wallet that deploys the contract. On testnet this wallet
# is also the owner. Later the ownership moves to your personal wallet with the two-step
# transfer (transferOwnership, then acceptOwnership).
# Format: 0x followed by 64 letters/numbers, with no quotes and no spaces.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Your personal wallet (public address, NOT a key) ---
# Where ownership goes later. Safe to fill in; it is only an address.
FINAL_OWNER_ADDRESS=

# --- Later: house agents and paid data feed (not built yet) ---
# The four house agents will use Circle developer-controlled wallets, so there are no
# raw agent keys in this file. These two values (SECRET) come from the Circle console.
# CIRCLE_API_KEY=
# CIRCLE_ENTITY_SECRET=

# --- Alerts when the runner stops (optional) ---
# A long random topic name for ntfy.sh (install the ntfy app on your phone and subscribe to it). Not a key, but anyone who knows it can read the alerts.
NTFY_TOPIC=

# --- Mainnet (real USDC): three separate wallets, never the same key twice ---
# MAINNET_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY (SECRET): deploys and owns the contracts. Only needed on the day of the deploy.
# RUNNER_PRIVATE_KEY (SECRET): the round runner's own wallet. It pushes prices and settles rounds, and the deploy script
#   sets its ADDRESS as the relay pusher. On mainnet the runner reads this key and nothing else. Fund it with a little USDC
#   for gas. It must not be the deployer, the final owner, a house agent, or any wallet people play with.
#   (On the testnet it is optional: without it the runner uses DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY.)
# MAINNET_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# RUNNER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- AI agents (Trend Follower, Contrarian, Chart Reader) ---
# GEMINI_API_KEY (SECRET): from Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com), free tier. Without it the three AI agents skip every round
#   ("Couldn't decide this round"). Coin Flipper does not need it.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional: the model, the price per million tokens used for the cost log (the free tier bills nothing; check ai.google.dev/pricing),
# and a safety limit of AI calls per UTC day (BTC 5m every round is about 864).
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# GEMINI_PRICE_IN_PER_M=0.30
# GEMINI_PRICE_OUT_PER_M=2.50
# GEMINI_MAX_CALLS_PER_DAY=1200

# --- Agent notes for the website (the reasons the AI agents give) ---
# Free Upstash Redis database (upstash.com). The runner WRITES with the normal token; the website (Vercel) only READS, so give Vercel
# the read-only token. Without these, the notes are written to data/agent-notes.jsonl and only a site running on this PC shows them.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# Which markets the AI agents play (names as on the site, comma separated, or "all"). Default: BTC/USD 5m only (about 864 AI calls a day if every
# round is played). Coin Flipper plays every market. On other markets the Contrarian only answers a real person's call.
# AI_MARKETS=BTC/USD 5m
# GEMINI_MAX_PER_MINUTE=10
